task:
AUTHORITATIVE FIRST V3 PRODUCT CHECKPOINT packet: implement the first real apps/web product slice on PR #601. Fetch the current remote migration/svelte-go-live-candidate head first. Expected dispatch head is 2eb6ba274ad33d4ddbd8f0d6ffbb891da1cf0a1f; if the remote has advanced, use the actual current head and preserve all unrelated work. Never reset, rebase, force-push, or rewrite history.

GOAL
Replace the generic migration placeholders with the first coherent ED-Finder V3 user journey: Explore/Finder -> real results + fresh Babylon spatial presentation -> select a system -> canonical Inspect detail. This must be a genuinely testable product checkpoint, not another foundation-only tranche.

AUTHORITIES / REQUIRED READING
Read CLAUDE.md and the current versions of: docs/development/v3-application-stack-decision.md, docs/development/v3-browser-validation-lanes.md, docs/development/v3-coordination-control-plane.md, docs/colonisation-redesign/spatial-platform-architecture-decision.md, current apps/web source/tests, and the current generated Hey API client. Preserve the locked stack and boundaries.

NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURE
- Svelte/SvelteKit owns routes, application/domain orchestration, panels, text, keyboard, accessibility and user state.
- Babylon owns spatial/GPU presentation only. No @babylonjs/* type or API may leak into components/domain contracts.
- All spatial interaction must pass through the renderer-neutral SpatialSceneContract / RuntimeCommand / RuntimeEvent boundary established on current #601. Do not bypass it with direct Babylon calls from Svelte.
- FastAPI/OpenAPI -> generated Hey API SDK -> handwritten apps/web API facade -> Svelte components remains authoritative. Components must not import generated modules directly or issue raw fetch for ordinary API operations.
- Preserve the lossless decimal-string Id64 lane end-to-end; never Number()/parseInt()/unary-plus canonical id64. Test values above Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER, including uint64 max where appropriate.
- Fresh Babylon visual/product design. Do NOT port or imitate the React/R3F map visual layout. Old React is behavioural/domain evidence only.
- Preserve WebGPU preference, WebGL2 fallback, hardened deferred/coalesced resize, runtime events, resource-loss/recovery plumbing, lifecycle/disposal and all current WP0/WP1/WP2 contracts.

ROUTING MODEL
Canonical product journeys remain /explore, /inspect, /plan, /review. Finder is the discovery capability inside Explore, not a separate canonical journey.
- /explore becomes the real discovery surface.
- /inspect?system=<lossless-id64> becomes the canonical cold-load system-detail journey.
- An Explore-context system overlay may remain as a convenience where useful, but it must reuse the same underlying detail model/component and must not replace /inspect as canonical detail.
- Closing an Explore overlay restores Explore context.
- Do not revive /finder/system/:id64 or other stale React routes as canonical V3 routes. Existing legacy hashes/shared links should normalize through the established compatibility layer.
- /plan and /review may remain honest placeholders in this packet, but must continue to route cleanly.

1. REAL EXPLORE / FINDER
Replace the generic Explore placeholder with a focused, accessible V3 discovery workspace. Use the current generated operations through the handwritten facade:
- autocompleteApiLocalAutocompleteGet for typeahead/autocomplete;
- localSearchEndpointApiLocalSearchPost for local/discovery results;
- use other existing typed map/search endpoints only where they materially support this first checkpoint and remain within scope.
Extend apps/web/src/lib/api/client.ts with typed application-facing wrappers for the required Explore operations instead of importing generated SDK calls in components. Do not reintroduce generic unknown/Record-based public app APIs when generated request/response types exist.

Minimum useful Explore behaviour:
- search input with keyboard-accessible typeahead;
- loading, empty, error and retry states;
- real results from the normal API;
- result rows/cards with system name, exact id64 and the most useful already-available summary fields without inventing data;
- selecting a result updates selected-system application/persistence context;
- a clear Inspect action navigates to /inspect?system=<id64>;
- keyboard operation for autocomplete/results and sensible focus movement;
- responsive desktop/laptop layout with honest mobile degradation; no need to port the old React layout.
Use TanStack Svelte Query for server/API state where appropriate and preserve the single configured query-client authority.

2. FRESH BABYLON GALAXY PRESENTATION
Turn the current non-product Babylon foundation into the first product spatial surface used by Explore. Keep /spatial-foundation diagnostic route if it remains useful, but Explore must host the real product spatial view.

Build the initial GalaxySceneContract from real Explore result data that contains valid spatial coordinates. Do not fabricate coordinates for systems that lack them. Establish a small renderer-neutral application mapper from typed API/domain results -> GalaxySceneContract / SpatialContribution.

Minimum first-checkpoint map behaviour:
- deterministic, fresh V3 visual language suitable for ED-Finder, not React parity;
- systems represented spatially from canonical Elite light-year coordinates;
- selected/active system state visibly distinguishable;
- result selection can issue renderer-neutral camera/focus command(s) where supported;
- picking a rendered system emits TARGET_PICKED through RuntimeEvent and updates Svelte/domain selection through a renderer-neutral handler;
- selecting/picking can expose/open Inspect without Babylon owning navigation;
- resize/remount/navigation remain stable;
- reduced-motion preference respected for any transition;
- no invented worldScale domain truth; renderer precision/scaling remains internal.

Implement only the command/event capabilities actually needed for this checkpoint (for example LOAD_SCENE, SET_CAMERA/FLY_TO as justified, PICK/TARGET_PICKED). Unsupported declared commands must continue to fail closed rather than pretend to execute. If current diagnostic adapter structure needs to evolve, keep Babylon-specific implementation behind apps/web/src/lib/spatial/babylon/*.

Do not expand into heatmaps, region hulls, timeline scrubber, cluster visualisation, routes, commander history or Planner map layers unless absolutely required for the minimal coherent checkpoint. Those are later product slices.

3. REAL CANONICAL INSPECT
Implement /inspect?system=<id64> as a real system-detail surface using the generated getSystem operation through the handwritten facade. Reuse/extract the current SystemOverlay detail implementation/model rather than maintaining divergent Explore-overlay and Inspect-page data logic.

Minimum Inspect behaviour:
- cold load by exact lossless id64;
- loading, not-found/invalid-id, API error and retry states;
- display the system name/id and useful typed fields already returned by the API;
- preserve exact id64 in links/state/DOM where exposed;
- accessible heading/focus structure;
- back/open-in-Explore affordance that does not corrupt selected-system context;
- Explore overlay and canonical Inspect share one underlying detail data/component contract.
Do not start Planner implementation here. A Plan action/link may route to the existing /plan placeholder with system context.

4. PRODUCT E2E / VISUAL ACCEPTANCE — NORMAL V3 LANE
Grow apps/web Cypress Product E2E into real behaviour, running the actual apps/web frontend + normal API/data path. Preserve Chrome + Firefox authority. Cypress validates product behaviour, NOT source code.

Required journeys:
- Explore loads and is usable;
- type/search -> real seeded result(s);
- keyboard typeahead/result selection;
- result selection updates selected-system context;
- Babylon spatial surface becomes renderer-ready and receives real scene content;
- selecting/picking a system remains synchronized with Svelte selection;
- Explore -> Inspect navigation loads the correct system detail;
- one deliberately unsafe-sized id64 survives route/client/detail handling exactly;
- resize/navigation/remount produces no uncaught renderer failure;
- accessibility smoke on the real Explore/Inspect journey;
- add a deliberately approved V3 visual assertion/screenshot only where deterministic and meaningful; old React screenshots/layout are not the oracle.

Keep retained React Cypress migration evidence separate and temporary. Do not add new React behavioural scope.

5. REVIEW LAB BOUNDARY — DO NOT POLISH LEGACY REACT
Do not spend this implementation packet fixing the old React Review Lab viewport failures. The current red legacy Review Lab is known migration debt and cannot be V3 Babylon acceptance.
However, prepare the new product slice so the immediately-following packet can retarget relevant deterministic Review Lab scenarios onto this same apps/web + Babylon frontend. Avoid implementation choices that require a separate Lab frontend/renderer. Do not collapse Product E2E and Review Lab into one lane.

6. DESIGN / UX QUALITY BAR
This is the first owner-visible product checkpoint, not a temporary engineer dashboard. Give Explore and Inspect a coherent fresh V3 presentation with clear hierarchy, usable spacing, responsive behaviour, accessible controls and deliberate empty/loading/error states. Keep it restrained and functional; do not over-design speculative features. Use the current Tailwind/CSS/design-token stack and accessible Svelte primitives already accepted by the repo. Do not copy React visual styling by default.

7. PRESERVE RELEASE / SAFETY BOUNDARIES
No deployment, Contabo mutation, production access, DNS, secrets, database/schema migration, data rewrite, OAuth secret change or destructive action. Do not alter the immutable release/preflight safety model except for narrowly necessary test wiring. Python 3.14 promotion hardening and nginx end-to-end deployment proof remain later pre-promotion work unless a tiny non-invasive contract change is directly required by this product slice.

VALIDATION
Run proportionate exact-head checks before sealing:
- resolve_project_state.py --strict;
- git diff --check;
- apps/web pnpm frozen install integrity;
- apps/web check/type, lint, format:check, unit tests, production build;
- shared package check/lint/test/build if touched;
- focused repository tests for generated-client boundary, Id64, routing/persistence/spatial boundary;
- normal apps/web Cypress Product E2E in available Chrome/Firefox browser support;
- verify no component/domain file imports @babylonjs/* or generated/* directly outside their allowed adapters/facade;
- verify no raw ordinary API fetch bypass was introduced.
Do not make legacy Review Lab green by changing old React product behaviour in this packet.

FINAL REPORT MUST INCLUDE
- exact starting and final SHA;
- files/components/routes added or materially changed;
- exact Explore API wrappers/typed models used;
- how API result data maps into renderer-neutral spatial scene data;
- RuntimeCommand/RuntimeEvent capabilities now exercised by product code;
- Inspect shared-detail implementation and route behaviour;
- Product E2E journeys and browser results;
- unsafe-id64 proof;
- any genuine blockers to the subsequent Review Lab rebase;
- explicit confirmation that no deployment/DB/DNS/secret/Contabo mutation occurred.

Do not start /plan or /review feature implementation beyond preserving clean routing/context. Do not port React visuals. Do not touch legacy Review Lab merely to make its current viewport checks green.
